Aim

To enable versioning in Amazon S3 and configure Cross-Region Replication between two S3 buckets in different AWS regions.

Part A — Enabling Versioning
Procedure
Step 1: Open S3 Bucket
Go to S3 Dashboard.
Select existing bucket.
Step 2: Enable Versioning
Open:
Properties tab
Scroll to:
Bucket Versioning
Click Edit.
Select:
Enable
Save changes.
Step 3: Upload Object

Upload file:

report.pdf
Step 4: Modify and Re-upload Same File
Edit file locally.
Upload same filename again.
Step 5: Delete Object
Select uploaded object.
Click Delete.
Observation
Version IDs generated automatically.
Older versions preserved after re-upload.
Delete marker created instead of permanent deletion.
Result

Successfully enabled versioning in S3 and verified object version preservation and recovery functionality.

Part B — Cross-Region Replication (CRR)
Procedure
Step 1: Create Destination Bucket
Go to S3 → Create Bucket.

Enter bucket name:

dest-crr-bucket
Choose different AWS region.
Create bucket.
Step 2: Enable Versioning on Destination Bucket
Open destination bucket.
Go to:
Properties → Bucket Versioning
Enable versioning.
Step 3: Configure Replication Rule
Open source bucket.
Go to:
Management tab
Click:
Replication Rules → Create Replication Rule
Step 4: Configure Rule Settings

Rule name:

academy-crr-rule
Status:
Enabled
Scope:
Apply to all objects
Step 5: Choose Destination Bucket
Select:
Another Bucket
Choose destination bucket.
Select AWS-managed/default IAM role.
Step 6: Save Replication Rule
Enable replication for:
New Objects
Save configuration.
Step 7: Verify Replication

Upload file to source bucket:

image.png
Open destination bucket.
Verify replicated object appears automatically.
Observation
Source and destination buckets created successfully.
Replication rule configured.
Newly uploaded objects replicated automatically to another AWS region.
Result

Successfully configured Cross-Region Replication between two S3 buckets in different AWS regions.
